# SFT execution status v0.108

2026-09-23. The private full-size controller/guardian/bootstrap lifecycle is
implemented and tested with syscall doubles. **No native Linux execution or
real import occurred, and Gate 5 remains incomplete.** No S3 payload access,
remote action, GPU use, commit or push occurred.

## Completed

The new full-size composition binds environment/control pins, input inventories
and worker receipts to the prepared entry. It derives memory/deadline limits
from the validated envelope and preserves the caller's original absolute
deadline through the controller and guardian. The frozen synthetic driver has a
hidden 220-second worker cap; the new driver does not reuse that cap or edit it.

The private bootstrap uses the frozen mount/isolation/privilege-drop helpers
and a fixed future staged entry. Its public API and the public composition API
are unconditionally closed with `host_guard_not_bound`; no approval flag opens
them. The earlier entry/preparation APIs remain unchanged and closed.

Review found two startup cleanup gaps before native execution. New start
handshakes now prevent controller/guardian and bootstrap work before the parent
owns the corresponding pidfd. A retained worker pidfd permits failure cleanup
even if the bootstrap stalls before cgroup attachment. Only owned pidfds and
the owned leaf cgroup are targeted; ambiguous signal/kill/close operations are
not retried. Exact READY, release ordering, zero exit status, matching receipt,
EOF and empty/removal checks remain necessary for a private success result.

Fork followed by pidfd acquisition is not atomic containment. If a child is
stopped before handle acquisition fails, cleanup may remain unconfirmed. This
limitation is explicitly retained; the tests do not establish complete native
containment, and no real execution path has been opened.

## Verification

**407 unique tests passed on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with zero failures,
errors or skips: 19 new bootstrap tests, 44 new composition tests, 48 prior
entry/guard tests and 296 unchanged regression tests. Native syscall boundaries
were doubled; privileged Linux test wrappers were not executed locally.

Ruff passed for all four new source/test files. A fresh isolated import loaded
no ML modules and confirmed the new public APIs reject. Independent review
rechecked the startup fixes and found no additional actionable defect.

All 21 readiness bindings, nine prior entry-development bindings and 78
qualified source hashes remain unchanged. Tracked and staged diffs are empty;
the successor files are local and unpushed, not part of the frozen native
qualification manifest.

