## Next work, before native execution

Finish the fixed staged entry/control loader and authenticated successor source
staging, connecting the bootstrap's fixed path to the existing private entry
adapter. Resolve cumulative native-write enforcement and its separately bounded
setup, scratch, OS and report-write scopes. These are existing missing parts,
not new policy gates.

Then the new lifecycle needs bounded native qualification plus the already
required host/runtime/source admission, source immutability or writer exclusion,
mount/resource readback, combined budgets and exact real-import authorization.
Local synthetic success cannot substitute for any of those observations.

The S3-backed pretrained checkpoint remains the recorded base; no current S3
availability claim is made. GPU and training remain off. The next local
entry/staging implementation does not require turning on a GPU.
